      "review_notes": "The prefix scan constructs the exact categorical CDF. A category-prefix comparison theorem identifies its quantiles with the original categorical rank partition, proving equality with WeightedChoice.law mapped to integer labels. The actual preprocessing scan is verified separately before composing the verified cumulative-table draw. Reviewer feedback replaced two binder-lemma forests by ClosedExp instances. Tests check scan[0,2,0,3]=[0,2,2,5], masses2/5 and3/5 at labels1 and3, infinite credit at zero-weight label0, singleton weight7 arbitrary-F expectation, and generic framing. The deterministic cumulativeTable helper is not counted separately."
